WEBVTT

00:01.947 --> 00:04.022
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:06.952 --> 00:09.788
<i>Hang on</i>, <i>Naomi</i>, <i>we'll get you</i>
<i>back here ASAP.</i>

00:09.830 --> 00:11.029
I'm sorry, George.

00:11.081 --> 00:13.698
Just tell my sister that I love her.

00:15.419 --> 00:19.037
- You killed Naomi!
- She wants her people to come here.

00:19.089 --> 00:22.373
And trust me, when they do,
we had better be far away from here.

00:22.426 --> 00:24.876
If you want to live,
you need to come with me.

00:24.928 --> 00:27.086
No one's going anywhere
with you, John.

00:34.396 --> 00:37.180
- What are you doing?
- Same thing I've always done, Kate.

00:37.232 --> 00:39.109
Surviving.

00:43.071 --> 00:44.698
Thunder's getting louder.

01:02.132 --> 01:03.508
<i>Sorry</i>, <i>Ron.</i>

01:04.468 --> 01:08.461
<i>Drone's got nothing but seafood</i>
<i>at 5</i>,<i>000 meters below.</i>

01:09.931 --> 01:12.257
<i>You pickin' anything up with yours?</i>

01:13.435 --> 01:14.634
<i>Zip.</i>

01:14.686 --> 01:17.856
<i>I'm trying to get her a peek</i>
<i>over this ridge as soon as I can.</i>

01:17.898 --> 01:20.265
<i>Sonar's pinging up something now.</i>

01:21.234 --> 01:24.070
- <i>You want to switch feeds?</i>
- <i>Roger that.</i>

01:26.448 --> 01:30.358
<i>I'm headed on a bearing</i>
<i>of about 137</i>

01:30.410 --> 01:33.194
<i>for the coordinates</i>
<i>we pulled off our guy's map</i>,

01:33.246 --> 01:35.280
<i>but don't hold your breath.</i>

01:38.085 --> 01:41.953
<i>Magnetometer's picking up a hell</i>
<i>of a lot of anomalies down here.</i>

01:42.589 --> 01:46.040
- <i>A chest full of doubloons?</i>
- <i>Keep dreaming</i>, <i>Ron.</i>

01:46.093 --> 01:49.179
<i>Let's swing around on the next grid</i>
<i>and recalibrate.</i>

01:51.306 --> 01:53.266
<i>Are you getting this?</i>

01:53.308 --> 01:55.633
<i>What? What's up?</i>

01:57.854 --> 02:00.857
<i>It... It's an airplane.</i>

02:06.571 --> 02:08.313
<i>Oh</i>, <i>my God.</i>

02:08.365 --> 02:11.733
<i>It's Oceanic 815.</i>

02:17.916 --> 02:20.919
<i>This haunting footage comes to us</i>
<i>from the</i> Christiane I,

02:20.961 --> 02:23.036
<i>a salvage vehicle in the Indian Ocean.</i>

02:23.088 --> 02:26.039
<i>For more than two months</i>
<i>it's been scouring the depths</i>

02:26.091 --> 02:30.303
<i>of the Sunda Trench off Bali in search</i>
<i>of the remains of sunken trading ships.</i>

02:30.345 --> 02:35.767
<i>Late last night the</i> Christiane <i>deployed</i>
<i>two remotely operated vehicles</i>, <i>RO Vs</i>,

02:35.809 --> 02:40.021
<i>that verified what the National</i>
<i>Transportation Safety Board long feared</i>,

02:40.063 --> 02:43.150
- <i>that the commercial...</i>
- How do you want your eggs, Dan?

02:43.191 --> 02:46.361
<i>...departing Sydney</i>, <i>Australia</i>,
<i>on September 22</i>, <i>2004.</i>

02:46.403 --> 02:49.156
So, what happened?
They found that missing plane?

02:49.197 --> 02:52.815
- Dan?
- <i>...Oceanic 815 did crash at sea.</i>

02:52.868 --> 02:56.037
- Dan?
- <i>Even with this tragic discovery...</i>

02:56.079 --> 02:58.999
Dan, why are you so upset?

03:00.834 --> 03:02.492
I don't know.

03:08.341 --> 03:11.125
- I can't find my vest!
- Check under your seat!

03:11.178 --> 03:13.169
- I already did!
- Get ready!

03:13.221 --> 03:14.598
Here, just take mine.

03:16.349 --> 03:18.258
Everybody out, now!

03:18.685 --> 03:21.261
Hey, genius! Go!

03:22.272 --> 03:23.346
Go!

04:10.862 --> 04:13.980
Hey. Are you Jack?

04:18.078 --> 04:19.788
Yeah. I'm Jack.

04:21.248 --> 04:22.791
Who are you?

04:26.461 --> 04:28.286
I'm Daniel Faraday.

04:32.008 --> 04:33.718
I'm here to rescue you.

05:06.501 --> 05:10.286
Hey, Dan. The chopper,
how many of you were on it?

05:10.338 --> 05:12.080
Four, including me.

05:12.132 --> 05:14.332
What happened to the rest of them?

05:15.761 --> 05:17.752
Yeah, yeah. I... have no idea.

05:17.804 --> 05:21.141
I don't know how many of them
were able to get out before it...

05:21.183 --> 05:23.758
...went down.
I jumped, and I lost my...

05:23.810 --> 05:25.437
What do you call it? My pack.

05:25.479 --> 05:27.720
My phone was in my bag.
If I had my phone...

05:27.773 --> 05:29.232
We have a phone.

05:31.109 --> 05:33.017
You have a phone.

05:34.613 --> 05:35.812
Thank you.

05:38.784 --> 05:41.317
- <i>Minkowski.</i>
- Hey, George, it's Daniel.

05:41.369 --> 05:45.071
<i>Dan? The chopper comm went dead.</i>
<i>What happened up there?</i>

05:45.123 --> 05:48.126
I don't know, George.
There was an electrical storm.

05:48.168 --> 05:50.577
All the instruments,
I think they went down.

05:50.629 --> 05:53.882
I made contact with some
of the survivors and...

05:53.924 --> 05:56.676
<i>Dan</i>, <i>am I on speaker?</i>

06:00.222 --> 06:02.755
Would you give me just one second?

06:08.021 --> 06:10.805
Don't worry. Naomi covered for us.

06:11.900 --> 06:13.975
They don't know what Locke did to her.

06:14.027 --> 06:15.268
You sure about that?

06:22.452 --> 06:25.622
OK, OK, so the boat hasn't heard
from anybody else yet,

06:25.664 --> 06:28.156
but these are GPS transponders.

06:28.208 --> 06:30.001
My team and I are wearing these.

06:30.043 --> 06:33.495
The transponders will send
the locations back to the ship,

06:33.547 --> 06:38.009
and the ship will send all locations
back to the phones.

06:39.052 --> 06:40.251
That's my signal,

06:40.303 --> 06:44.005
and we'll hopefully get the signals
from the rest of the team soon.

06:44.057 --> 06:47.592
- Will you help me find them?
- Absolutely.

06:47.644 --> 06:48.718
OK. Thank you.

06:52.065 --> 06:54.182
Where are the rest of your people?

06:54.943 --> 06:58.394
- Most of them are back at the beach.
- Most of them?

07:13.378 --> 07:17.288
Dude, what's wrong with you?
You're gonna get struck by lightning.

07:21.178 --> 07:22.919
The storm is about to pass, Hugo.

07:22.971 --> 07:25.171
It's a freakin' monsoon. We gotta...

07:31.938 --> 07:33.398
Let's go.

07:44.034 --> 07:45.525
Why are you going east?

07:45.577 --> 07:48.246
I thought you said the barracks
were due south.

07:48.288 --> 07:50.864
Because we have to make
a little detour first.

07:50.916 --> 07:54.784
- Detour to what?
- There's a cabin I have to go to.

07:54.836 --> 07:57.245
I thought the cabin was back that way.

07:58.173 --> 07:59.664
What did you say, Hugo?

08:03.512 --> 08:06.921
I thought you were talking about
the airplane cabin.

08:09.518 --> 08:12.270
Why are we wasting our time
going to some shack?

08:12.312 --> 08:14.387
- Because we're supposed to.
- Right.

08:14.439 --> 08:18.057
Like you were supposed to throw
a knife into that Naomi chick's back?

08:22.906 --> 08:26.399
You mind who you're getting
your orders from, Colonel Kurtz?

08:27.786 --> 08:29.413
I got 'em from Walt.

08:43.635 --> 08:45.595
Jack still isn't back.

08:48.223 --> 08:49.850
Anything?

08:49.891 --> 08:53.009
No. But it's a big island.

08:53.061 --> 08:55.929
The freighter could be approaching
from the other side.

08:55.981 --> 08:58.014
That's the spirit.

09:00.944 --> 09:03.436
Juliet, you lived amongst the Others.

09:03.488 --> 09:06.898
Why would Ben say the people
coming here intend to do us harm?

09:06.950 --> 09:08.691
Because he's a liar,

09:08.744 --> 09:11.663
and he's trying to scare us.
That's what Ben does.

09:13.874 --> 09:17.617
Or because the people coming here
intend to do us harm.

09:20.797 --> 09:22.956
How many guns do you have left?

09:36.646 --> 09:37.720
Hey.

09:38.106 --> 09:39.733
Is that from your chopper?

09:42.444 --> 09:44.154
Yeah, yeah, that... Yeah.

09:44.196 --> 09:47.480
They reduced the weight load
when they started going down.

09:48.366 --> 09:50.567
Guess that's why they pushed me out.

09:52.454 --> 09:53.945
What's this for?

09:59.002 --> 10:02.287
I'm not in charge of packing.

10:03.298 --> 10:05.832
- You're not, huh?
- We should...

10:05.884 --> 10:09.054
Hey, Daniel, why'd you bring the gun?

10:15.060 --> 10:16.718
As a precaution.

10:17.312 --> 10:19.387
Precaution against what?

10:24.402 --> 10:25.977
OK, see...

10:27.906 --> 10:30.659
Rescuing you and your people...

10:31.952 --> 10:35.612
...I can't really say
it's our primary objective.

10:37.290 --> 10:39.115
Then what is?

10:47.300 --> 10:49.125
It's Miles.

10:49.177 --> 10:51.878
It's Miles. Come on.

10:51.930 --> 10:55.507
What the hell you mean
you saw Walt? In a dream?

10:55.559 --> 10:57.675
No dream. It was Walt.

10:57.727 --> 11:00.595
Only... taller.

11:00.647 --> 11:02.931
Taller? Like a giant?

11:06.278 --> 11:10.063
- OK, what exactly did Walt tell you?
- He said I had work to do,

11:10.115 --> 11:14.192
that I had to stop this woman Naomi from
bringing the rest of her people here.

11:14.244 --> 11:16.361
You didn't ask him follow-up questions?

11:16.413 --> 11:19.197
Ben shot me and left me for dead.
Walt saved my life

11:19.249 --> 11:22.252
so I pretty much took him at his word.

11:22.294 --> 11:23.670
He shot you,

11:23.712 --> 11:27.288
yet here you are, fit as a fiddle,
tromping through the jungle.

11:30.135 --> 11:31.762
The bullet went in one side,

11:31.803 --> 11:33.628
came out the other.

11:41.271 --> 11:44.191
I'd probably be dead
if I still had a kidney there.

11:45.358 --> 11:46.985
Anything else?

12:15.013 --> 12:16.296
He's down there.

12:18.308 --> 12:19.632
Hey, Miles!

12:22.938 --> 12:24.012
Miles!

12:38.161 --> 12:40.361
Is he dead?

12:40.414 --> 12:41.988
Back up, handsome.

12:44.501 --> 12:46.743
Miles, take it easy, it's OK.

12:46.795 --> 12:49.078
They're here to help us. It's OK, Miles.

12:49.131 --> 12:51.915
- They're just trying to help.
- Back away from him!

12:51.967 --> 12:54.584
- Hands where I can see 'em!
- Kate, it's all right.

12:54.636 --> 12:55.919
It's OK.

12:57.305 --> 12:58.463
So you're Kate.

13:00.725 --> 13:03.051
You want to tell me where Naomi is?

13:04.688 --> 13:07.222
- What?
- Naomi, the woman you killed.

13:09.443 --> 13:10.517
Where is she?

13:20.078 --> 13:23.571
<i>For the friends and families</i>
<i>of the passengers of Oceanic 815</i>,

13:23.623 --> 13:26.908
<i>this can only be described</i>
<i>as the worst-case scenario.</i>

13:26.960 --> 13:29.661
<i>With the plane accounted for</i>
<i>and a salvage mission unlikely</i>,

13:29.713 --> 13:33.925
<i>authorities are confirming</i>
<i>all 324 passengers dead.</i>

13:48.106 --> 13:50.682
Ms Gardner, I'm Miles Straume.

13:50.734 --> 13:54.310
- We spoke on the phone earlier.
- Oh, please come in.

14:06.750 --> 14:10.326
- Which room is it?
- Upstairs at the end of the hall.

14:10.921 --> 14:14.455
I get paid in advance.
Two hundred, cash only.

14:14.508 --> 14:15.790
You told me a hundred...

14:15.842 --> 14:19.919
That was before my buddy at the police
said your grandson was murdered.

14:21.223 --> 14:23.256
It's gonna be two hundred.

14:23.975 --> 14:25.300
Fine.

14:49.042 --> 14:51.795
No matter what you hear,
don't come up.

15:33.795 --> 15:37.539
You're not doing your grandmother
any good staying here, man.

15:37.591 --> 15:39.999
You're causing her a lot of pain.

15:44.639 --> 15:48.007
I... I want to go downstairs
and tell her you've gone,

15:48.059 --> 15:51.469
but the only way
I'm gonna be able to do that

15:51.521 --> 15:54.097
is if you tell me where it is.

15:59.821 --> 16:01.312
So where is it?

16:38.777 --> 16:40.153
You can go now.

16:47.285 --> 16:48.568
Did it work?

16:50.080 --> 16:51.237
Yeah.

16:53.166 --> 16:54.991
He's at peace now.

17:03.343 --> 17:04.584
Here.

17:06.054 --> 17:07.879
You get a refund. Half off.

17:09.015 --> 17:11.090
Wasn't as tricky as I thought.

17:14.271 --> 17:15.981
Thank you.

17:16.440 --> 17:17.816
Thank you.

17:19.693 --> 17:22.477
Miles. Miles!
Hey, what are you doing?

17:22.529 --> 17:24.896
What are you doing?
These are good people.

17:24.948 --> 17:26.940
Why'd Naomi use the damn code? Yeah.

17:26.992 --> 17:29.828
Remember when she said,
"Tell my sister I love her?"

17:29.870 --> 17:31.361
She doesn't have a sister.

17:32.497 --> 17:34.322
That's what we're supposed to say

17:34.374 --> 17:37.377
if we get captured,
have a gun to our head.

17:37.419 --> 17:40.954
Like right now Jack here would say,
"Tell my sister I love her."

17:41.006 --> 17:43.706
- You get it?
- We didn't kill your friend.

17:45.010 --> 17:49.003
- Then take me to her body.
- Miles, what about Charlotte? Frank?

17:49.055 --> 17:52.142
- Take me to Naomi.
- Naomi was killed, but not by us.

17:52.184 --> 17:54.936
It was a man by the name of John Locke.

17:54.978 --> 17:58.012
- He's not with us anymore.
- Kate, if I have to ask again...

17:58.064 --> 18:01.349
- Even if I took you to her body...
- I'll know!

18:03.153 --> 18:05.113
Now take me to her body.

18:21.421 --> 18:22.495
Alex.

18:24.966 --> 18:26.082
Alex, hey.

18:27.302 --> 18:29.669
- What?
- Something I need to tell you.

18:29.721 --> 18:31.598
Keep your mouth shut, Mr Linus.

18:32.641 --> 18:37.302
Karl. If you're gonna sleep with
my daughter I insist you call me Ben.

18:38.271 --> 18:41.472
Easy, kid. Guy's just
trying to get in your head.

18:43.568 --> 18:45.226
Go take a walk or something.

18:51.743 --> 18:55.956
- Mind if I ask you a question, James?
- Yeah, I do.

18:56.623 --> 18:58.166
Why'd you leave Kate behind?

18:59.793 --> 19:01.868
You're wasting your time, Yoda.

19:03.046 --> 19:05.538
I know it's not pleasant,
but let's face it,

19:05.590 --> 19:07.957
you really don't stand a chance now.

19:09.094 --> 19:10.470
Chance at what?

19:10.512 --> 19:13.796
James, look at yourself.

19:13.849 --> 19:17.300
Yes, on this island,
you're brave, daring, handsome.

19:17.352 --> 19:20.470
You're someone,
but if you left with them...

19:21.440 --> 19:25.058
...back in the real world
a lowlife scam artist like you

19:25.110 --> 19:28.144
could never compete
with a first-class surgeon.

19:29.156 --> 19:33.066
I think Kate was really upset when
you made your choice to come with us.

19:35.370 --> 19:37.862
Thank God she has Jack there
to comfort her...

19:40.834 --> 19:42.116
James!

19:43.211 --> 19:44.869
- Don't!
- Don't what?!

19:45.797 --> 19:48.498
Anyone want to tell me
why we're keeping him alive?

19:48.550 --> 19:52.377
We're keeping him alive because
he's been on this island longer than us,

19:52.429 --> 19:54.754
because he has information we need.

19:54.806 --> 19:57.590
Apart from his mouth,
he's completely harmless.

19:57.642 --> 19:59.551
His mouth put that hole in your gut?

20:00.812 --> 20:04.889
OK, James, let's execute him
right here, right now,

20:04.941 --> 20:07.058
in front of his daughter.

20:26.421 --> 20:29.372
It's only a matter of time
before he gets us, Johnny.

20:30.467 --> 20:33.877
And I'll bet he's already figured out
how he's gonna do it.

20:36.264 --> 20:37.808
So you walk him.

21:04.835 --> 21:06.409
What's he doing?

21:07.963 --> 21:09.423
The light...

21:09.464 --> 21:12.081
...is strange out here, isn't it?

21:12.134 --> 21:16.294
It's kind of like it doesn't scatter

21:16.346 --> 21:17.670
quite right.

21:20.809 --> 21:22.842
Dan?

21:22.894 --> 21:24.719
Your name is Dan, right?

21:26.690 --> 21:31.518
Listen, Dan, I know that you don't
want anybody to get hurt, right?

21:31.570 --> 21:34.604
So why don't you just put that away.

21:36.742 --> 21:40.787
Because Miles would kill me.

21:41.371 --> 21:43.404
We're just trying to help...

21:43.457 --> 21:45.333
Kate, you're wasting your breath.

21:45.375 --> 21:48.044
Just let this play out
and see what happens, OK?

21:53.884 --> 21:56.887
They didn't kill her.
It happened like they said it did.

21:58.263 --> 22:01.433
It's Charlotte. She's only
three kilometres from here.

22:01.475 --> 22:03.383
All right. Let's go get her.

22:05.854 --> 22:08.638
- I said let's go.
- You need to put the guns down.

22:08.690 --> 22:10.974
- What?
- Put the guns down.

22:12.569 --> 22:15.739
- Now why would I do that?
- Our friends are in the jungle now

22:15.781 --> 22:18.481
holding a gun at your head
and his head.

22:19.284 --> 22:22.318
I'll forget about the misunderstanding.
Put the guns down.

22:22.370 --> 22:24.863
How stupid do you think I am?

22:35.425 --> 22:36.916
I don't know, Miles.

22:38.345 --> 22:40.962
How stupid are you?

23:15.424 --> 23:18.510
How many different languages
do you have to read that in

23:18.552 --> 23:20.512
before you believe it's true?

23:20.554 --> 23:22.837
How many different languages are there?

23:27.310 --> 23:29.104
He wants to know if we're lost.

23:29.146 --> 23:32.931
Remind him people in our line of work
are terrible at keeping secrets.

23:32.983 --> 23:34.224
I know about the dig.

23:38.572 --> 23:42.232
- He said the site is closed.
- Then tell him to open it.

23:58.216 --> 23:59.593
Dinosaur?

24:00.927 --> 24:02.752
Not by a few million years.

24:02.804 --> 24:04.681
It's an <i>Ursus maritimus.</i>

24:04.723 --> 24:07.215
Wait, <i>ursus</i>, as in bear?

24:09.394 --> 24:11.188
As in polar bear.

24:13.732 --> 24:17.433
Charlotte, we're in the desert.
This is a hoax, right?

24:21.198 --> 24:23.314
He wants to know what
you're doing with the hammer.

24:23.366 --> 24:24.607
Excavating.

24:30.957 --> 24:32.782
Is that a collar?

25:53.790 --> 25:55.167
Hi.

25:56.918 --> 25:58.952
Hi yourself.

26:06.803 --> 26:08.878
We were worried
when you didn't get back,

26:08.930 --> 26:11.881
so we went out to the cockpit
and tracked you from there.

26:11.933 --> 26:13.925
Thanks for that, for what it's worth.

26:13.977 --> 26:15.051
Don't mention it.

26:15.103 --> 26:18.440
Somebody could've told me
the cavalry were here.

26:19.191 --> 26:21.724
I gave you that... wink.

26:24.613 --> 26:26.437
What are your names?

26:26.490 --> 26:28.898
I'm Daniel Faraday,
and this is Miles...

26:28.950 --> 26:30.525
Don't tell him my last name.

26:31.745 --> 26:33.538
I guess this is just Miles.

26:33.580 --> 26:36.583
- What do you do for a living, Daniel?
- I'm a physicist.

26:36.625 --> 26:38.533
I guess you can call me a physicist.

26:38.585 --> 26:40.827
I don't really like being pigeonholed...

26:40.879 --> 26:43.799
Dan, you say one more word
and I'll break your fingers.

26:43.840 --> 26:46.593
- What do you do, Miles?
- I collect soil samples.

26:46.635 --> 26:49.085
That's nice. Maybe you can help me.

26:49.137 --> 26:51.588
You say you're not here
on a rescue mission,

26:51.640 --> 26:54.309
and the world at large
believes us to be dead.

26:55.268 --> 26:56.978
But here we are, alive and well,

26:57.020 --> 26:59.804
and you don't seem
remotely surprised to see us.

26:59.856 --> 27:04.236
Oh, my God, you guys were on
Oceanic flight 815! Wow!

27:04.277 --> 27:05.935
That better?

27:10.117 --> 27:12.150
I can't believe you're alive.

27:14.329 --> 27:15.987
How many of you are there?

27:17.457 --> 27:19.282
Why do you want to know?

27:20.168 --> 27:21.711
Why wouldn't I want to know?

27:25.799 --> 27:27.957
Forty-eight of us survived the crash.

27:28.009 --> 27:30.126
That's not counting the tail section.

27:30.178 --> 27:32.170
- They're pretty much dead...
- Hugo.

27:33.849 --> 27:36.716
So you've all been living here
this entire time?

27:38.228 --> 27:39.636
Is that your baby?

27:40.897 --> 27:42.555
Yeah. This is Aaron.

27:42.607 --> 27:44.568
Did you have him here on the island?

27:45.610 --> 27:47.268
That's amazing.

27:48.572 --> 27:52.440
Well, I've got about a million
more questions I want to ask you,

27:52.492 --> 27:55.360
but they can wait until
we get you back to the freighter.

27:55.412 --> 27:58.112
We've all got
one of these transponders,

27:58.165 --> 28:00.615
so if we sit tight
they're gonna be here soon.

28:00.667 --> 28:03.587
This team of yours,
how many of you are there?

28:04.588 --> 28:05.870
Four, including me.

28:06.923 --> 28:08.998
What happened to your helicopter?

28:09.050 --> 28:11.835
I don't know. The pilot
was trying to put it down.

28:11.887 --> 28:14.420
- Where?
- I don't know.

28:14.973 --> 28:17.465
I had to jump. It was chaos.

28:19.603 --> 28:21.396
I'm lucky to be alive.

28:24.733 --> 28:26.443
Get up. You're coming with us.

28:27.277 --> 28:30.854
What? Why? We need to stay
where we are so they can find us.

28:30.906 --> 28:32.616
See, there's your problem.

28:32.657 --> 28:34.618
We don't want to be found.

28:39.706 --> 28:42.115
I wouldn't mess around with that
if I were you.

28:42.167 --> 28:44.450
It can't hurt to try and call
someone else.

28:44.503 --> 28:46.244
Oh, it can hurt.

28:46.296 --> 28:49.049
- What'd you do?
- I didn't do anything.

28:51.218 --> 28:52.844
Your friend Charlotte,

28:52.886 --> 28:54.513
she's moving.

28:55.764 --> 28:57.390
And she's moving fast.

29:01.103 --> 29:03.261
She's running from something.

29:30.340 --> 29:32.832
According to this she's right here.

29:33.552 --> 29:35.627
- Charlotte?
- Charlotte!

29:45.147 --> 29:46.857
Over there, over there.

29:56.116 --> 29:57.190
Vincent.

30:01.371 --> 30:02.612
Locke's got her.

30:19.139 --> 30:21.631
<i>We want to caution our viewers</i>
<i>the images</i>

30:21.683 --> 30:26.177
<i>they are about to see are graphic.</i>
<i>Viewer discretion is advised.</i>

30:26.229 --> 30:32.517
<i>Authorities released footage of the</i>
<i>sunken remains of Oceanic flight 815.</i>

30:32.569 --> 30:36.271
<i>The National Transportation</i>
<i>Safety Board has set up a hotline</i>

30:36.323 --> 30:39.607
<i>for family members</i>
<i>of the Oceanic victims.</i>

30:39.659 --> 30:43.528
<i>The NTSB has begun</i>
<i>the victim identification process.</i>

30:44.748 --> 30:47.615
<i>We have confirmation</i>
<i>that this is the pilot</i>,

30:47.667 --> 30:50.076
<i>Captain Seth Norris.</i>

30:50.128 --> 30:54.122
<i>In a statement</i>,
<i>the NTSB said that</i>,

30:54.174 --> 30:56.749
<i>"Due to the sheer depth of the wreck...</i>

30:57.928 --> 31:00.879
<i>...recovery of the bodies</i>
<i>would be next to impossible.</i>

31:00.931 --> 31:04.101
<i>We can only hope that identification</i>
<i>will provide closure</i>

31:04.142 --> 31:06.259
<i>to the families of the victims."</i>

31:17.697 --> 31:20.982
<i>National Transportation Safety Board</i>,
<i>Oceanic hotline.</i>

31:21.034 --> 31:22.828
Let me speak to your supervisor.

31:22.869 --> 31:25.486
<i>Yes</i>, <i>sir. Are you a family member</i>
<i>of the deceased?</i>

31:25.539 --> 31:27.864
No, but I got some information
on the crash.

31:27.916 --> 31:30.585
- May I speak to your supervisor?
- <i>If you could...</i>

31:30.627 --> 31:32.702
I'm staring at the television now,

31:32.754 --> 31:36.581
you're broadcasting footage and saying
that's the pilot, Seth Norris.

31:36.633 --> 31:37.707
<i>Yes</i>, <i>sir?</i>

31:37.759 --> 31:39.501
That's not him.

31:41.930 --> 31:43.306
<i>Please hold.</i>

31:44.641 --> 31:46.925
- <i>Who am I speaking with?</i>
- Doesn't matter.

31:46.977 --> 31:49.928
You're showing footage of Seth Norris.
That's not him.

31:49.980 --> 31:54.025
He married his high school sweetheart,
always wore his wedding ring.

31:54.067 --> 31:55.975
There's no ring on that body.

31:56.027 --> 32:00.438
- <i>Sir</i>, <i>it's likely the ring fell off...</i>
- I'm telling you that is not him.

32:01.366 --> 32:05.068
<i>And how exactly is it that you know</i>
<i>all about Captain Norris?</i>

32:06.621 --> 32:10.532
Because I was supposed to be flying
Oceanic 815 on that day.

33:33.708 --> 33:34.824
That's them.

33:34.876 --> 33:37.035
That's somebody from my team.

33:42.050 --> 33:45.387
What's wrong with you people?
We're here because of you.

33:45.429 --> 33:47.962
I just almost died jumping out
of a helicopter

33:48.014 --> 33:49.923
because you called us for help.

33:50.392 --> 33:53.176
Maybe we should see
who launched that flare.

33:53.228 --> 33:55.897
- They could be hurt, John.
- She's lying.

33:55.939 --> 33:58.014
Whatever they came for, it isn't us.

33:58.066 --> 34:00.350
We keep moving forward as planned.

34:00.402 --> 34:02.727
Who are we to argue
with Taller Ghost Walt?

34:02.779 --> 34:05.480
- Do whatever you want.
- I want you to come with us.

34:05.532 --> 34:07.325
I'm not asking for permission.

34:07.367 --> 34:10.370
If you think you're gonna stop me
from getting to my...

34:17.043 --> 34:19.494
What did you do, you son of a bitch?

34:28.680 --> 34:31.047
- The vest.
- What?

34:31.099 --> 34:32.507
Vest.

34:32.559 --> 34:33.716
Vest.

34:48.075 --> 34:50.233
- Is he alive?
- He's got a pulse.

34:50.285 --> 34:52.079
Frank?

34:52.913 --> 34:54.790
Frank. Hey, hey.

34:54.831 --> 34:56.208
Frank!

34:58.835 --> 35:00.994
Are you OK? What happened?

35:03.507 --> 35:07.125
- We got struck by lightning.
- Frank, where's Charlotte?

35:07.177 --> 35:10.013
She bailed out just...
before we went down.

35:10.055 --> 35:12.839
- I don't know where she is.
- Where's the chopper?

35:12.891 --> 35:14.518
I saw a cow.

35:18.396 --> 35:21.149
Lapidus, where's the chopper?
Where did it crash?

35:21.191 --> 35:24.111
Crash? What the hell kind of pilot
do you think I am?

35:24.152 --> 35:27.020
I put her down safe and sound
right over there.

35:57.018 --> 35:59.010
So this is the team?

35:59.062 --> 36:01.304
Have you familiarised yourself
with their profiles?

36:01.356 --> 36:05.902
Unfortunately, yes. These are the wrong
people for a mission like this.

36:05.944 --> 36:08.978
None of them have field experience,
military training.

36:09.030 --> 36:12.398
You can't just drop them in
unprotected. It'll be a disaster.

36:12.451 --> 36:14.776
They are not unprotected.
They have you.

36:14.828 --> 36:17.320
There's only so much I can do.

36:18.248 --> 36:21.032
Your modesty is positively charming.

36:21.084 --> 36:24.994
This is a high-risk covert op
in unstable territory.

36:25.046 --> 36:28.081
It's dodgy enough without
having to baby-sit a head case,

36:28.133 --> 36:30.291
ghostbuster, anthropologist and drunk.

36:30.343 --> 36:32.460
To be fair he is also
a pretty good pilot.

36:32.512 --> 36:33.889
It's madness.

36:33.930 --> 36:36.381
What if we find survivors from 815?

36:36.433 --> 36:38.800
- There were no survivors.
- Yes, I know.

36:38.852 --> 36:42.345
- But what if there are survivors?
- There were no survivors

36:42.397 --> 36:44.107
of Oceanic 815.

36:44.149 --> 36:47.235
Don't ask questions.
Just do what you were hired for.

36:47.277 --> 36:50.447
Every member of this team
was selected for a specific purpose.

36:50.489 --> 36:53.658
Everything relies on you
getting them in, getting them out

36:53.700 --> 36:56.317
and preventing anyone
from getting killed.

36:56.369 --> 36:58.246
Think you can do that?

37:00.957 --> 37:02.334
Sure.

37:02.375 --> 37:04.086
Why not?

37:24.648 --> 37:25.722
Well?

37:25.774 --> 37:29.559
There's some minor damage, but
the mechanical systems are intact.

37:30.362 --> 37:33.031
- So it will fly, then?
- Absolutely.

37:34.366 --> 37:35.940
Can I have the phone now?

37:36.993 --> 37:39.527
Tell you what. I'll give you the phone

37:39.579 --> 37:42.280
if you tell me what you people
are doing here.

37:42.332 --> 37:45.585
I'll tell you what we're doing here
if you give me the phone.

37:49.881 --> 37:52.123
Don't say anything about your sister.

37:54.636 --> 37:57.128
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Regina, it's Miles.

37:57.180 --> 37:58.922
I need to talk to Minkowski.

37:58.974 --> 38:01.424
<i>Minkowski can't come</i>
<i>to the phone right now.</i>

38:02.269 --> 38:04.229
It's important. Go get him.

38:04.271 --> 38:06.721
<i>Miles</i>, <i>he can't come</i>
<i>to the phone right now.</i>

38:07.732 --> 38:09.974
All right, have him call me
when he can.

38:10.026 --> 38:11.434
<i>I gotta go.</i>

38:14.906 --> 38:16.783
Whoa! What are you doing with her?

38:16.825 --> 38:20.401
- We're taking her with us.
- What's the point? That's not Naomi.

38:20.454 --> 38:23.071
- It's just meat.
- We can't just leave her here.

38:23.123 --> 38:24.531
Miles is right.

38:25.208 --> 38:28.462
We burned up most of the fuel
flying around that storm.

38:28.503 --> 38:31.204
We barely got enough
to get back to the freighter.

38:31.256 --> 38:33.331
We won't carry unnecessary weight.

38:33.383 --> 38:36.084
I'll take her on the next run.

38:36.136 --> 38:38.096
I promise, Dan.

38:41.224 --> 38:44.592
There's a blanket over there
by my backpack. Would you get it?

38:45.520 --> 38:47.481
Look as bad as it feels?

38:47.522 --> 38:49.232
How bad does it feel?

38:51.443 --> 38:53.560
- What's your name again?
- Juliet.

38:54.613 --> 38:57.365
Juliet. Juliet what?

38:58.408 --> 38:59.816
Juliet Burke.

38:59.868 --> 39:01.828
Juliet Burke.

39:03.413 --> 39:05.373
You weren't on that plane, were you?

39:08.585 --> 39:10.076
Miles!

39:11.755 --> 39:12.829
Yeah?

39:12.881 --> 39:16.218
This is Juliet,
and she was not on the plane.

39:17.594 --> 39:18.835
What?!

39:20.055 --> 39:21.129
You sure?

39:21.181 --> 39:23.965
You know how many times
I studied that damn manifest?

39:24.017 --> 39:27.051
There's no Juliet Burke on that plane.
She's a native.

39:27.604 --> 39:29.564
Really? Where is he?!

39:29.606 --> 39:31.598
- Back off!
- Where's who?

39:31.650 --> 39:34.486
You want to know why we're here?
I'll tell you why.

39:36.780 --> 39:39.449
We're here for Benjamin Linus.

39:45.414 --> 39:47.405
Now where is he?

39:48.542 --> 39:50.450
James, listen to me, please.

39:50.502 --> 39:53.536
- Keep your mouth shut.
- Are you OK?

39:53.588 --> 39:56.925
I feel like I've got a cinder block
on my chest, but I'll survive.

39:56.967 --> 40:00.168
Sorry you got shot.
I didn't intend for that to happen.

40:00.220 --> 40:03.505
Really? It seemed like you were
about to shoot me yourself.

40:04.433 --> 40:06.226
What good would you be to me dead?

40:06.268 --> 40:09.020
I feel much more comfortable now.
Thanks.

40:11.982 --> 40:15.558
I guess this is the part where
I'm supposed to say, "I told you so."

40:16.778 --> 40:18.353
James, I stand corrected.

40:19.030 --> 40:20.939
You want me to do it?

40:20.991 --> 40:24.161
No, it's my mess. I'll clean up.

40:27.748 --> 40:30.584
- Wait!
- Danielle, escort Alex away from here.

40:30.625 --> 40:32.367
- Let's go. Come on.
- No!

40:32.419 --> 40:33.910
She's right. Let's go.

40:33.962 --> 40:36.287
Anyone who doesn't want to see this
should leave now.

40:36.339 --> 40:37.747
We should talk about this...

40:37.799 --> 40:40.969
What if one of those bullets
hit you or the baby?

40:41.011 --> 40:42.669
John, listen.

40:44.097 --> 40:46.339
I have information that you need.

40:47.225 --> 40:48.508
I have answers.

40:51.855 --> 40:53.565
What is the monster?

40:54.691 --> 40:57.392
- What?
- The black smoke, the monster.

40:58.028 --> 40:59.404
What is it?

41:00.614 --> 41:02.021
I don't know.

41:03.283 --> 41:06.369
- Goodbye, Benjamin.
- Her name is Charlotte Lewis!

41:10.707 --> 41:12.824
Charlotte Staples Lewis.

41:14.044 --> 41:17.537
Born July 2, 1979,
Essex, England.

41:17.589 --> 41:20.842
Parents David and Jeannette.
Eldest of three, all girls.

41:21.593 --> 41:23.303
She was raised in Bromsgrove.

41:23.345 --> 41:25.503
Did her undergraduate studies at Kent.

41:25.555 --> 41:28.673
Took her Ph.D.
in cultural anthropology at Oxford.

41:28.725 --> 41:31.478
She's here with two other
team members and a pilot.

41:31.520 --> 41:34.606
Their names: Daniel Faraday,
Miles Straume,

41:34.648 --> 41:36.389
Frank Lapidus.

41:44.324 --> 41:47.192
Your instinct was right, John.

41:47.244 --> 41:49.444
These people are a threat.

41:50.539 --> 41:54.699
If you shoot me, you'll never know
how great a threat they were.

41:54.751 --> 41:57.587
Because I know what they're doing here.

41:57.629 --> 41:59.287
I know what they want.

42:00.215 --> 42:01.758
What do they want?

42:03.844 --> 42:05.960
Me, James. They want me.

42:14.646 --> 42:16.679
How do you know all this?

42:21.027 --> 42:23.947
Because I have a man on their boat.
